{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"acidic-ferreous-mole","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nDiscovered while debugging grindable-deviant-angwantibo. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::_collect_node_ids` launches a real nested pytest collection subprocess without `--basetemp`. The confirmed sibling mechanism is pytest session shutdown traversing the shared numbered temp root in `cleanup_numbered_dir`/`rmtree`, which can delete or stall on another run's temp tree. The fixed `_store_isolation` helper does not cover this independent caller.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a RED regression that gives the nested collection subprocess a poisoned shared numbered temp root and proves a pre-existing sentinel survives unchanged.\n- Pass a caller-owned private `--basetemp` directory to `_collect_node_ids` without changing its collection selection, stdout parsing, return-code contract, or timeout.\n- Prove GREEN, seed the omitted-basetemp mutation back to RED, and run focused plus repository gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The regression fails on the current implementation because nested collection removes or traverses the shared numbered-root sentinel.\n- [ ] `_collect_node_ids` runs nested pytest with a private basetemp owned by the caller.\n- [ ] The held-out regression passes and the exact-defect mutation returns it to RED.\n- [ ] Existing workflow-parity tests pass.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` pass.","id":"444d-62ff-2c3c-42a9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["test","flaky"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Give parity collection subprocess a private pytest basetemp"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786898143082505001,"uuid":"f452377c-9206-46b6-8438-77fe269fddfd"}